./novel/chapters/ch-01/scenes/s-002.md:13:Thomas Reed was in the service room, his hands carrying the faint grains of his work. He said he’d been in the workshop across the square until just before eleven and that a neighbour could confirm it. He spoke quickly, with an impatience that shortened his answers, and kept rubbing the pad of his thumb and forefinger together in that restless way of men who handle small gears. When I asked about the disputed sale he gave a clipped account and shut the subject down.
